From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:24:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add the Indian Ocean yellowfin case study and an
 age-selectivity article

Bundled data io_yft_data, io_yft_parameters, io_yft_map and
io_yft_reference (exported from the SS3 conversion in
N-DucharmeBarth/wcpfc-bet-single-region; the reference now carries SS3's
age_selex patterns and parameters), with stored fits:

- io_yft_c2_fit.rds: C2, length-based selectivity (refitted on this
  branch, objective 14406.585)
- io_yft_age_fit.rds: A, age-based selectivity (sel_basis_f = 2) started
  from SS3's parameters, C2's map
- io_yft_age_ss3_fit.rds: A-SS3, as A, estimating every selectivity
  parameter SS3 estimated

Two articles: "Comparing opal with Stock Synthesis" and "Length- or
age-based selectivity". Both read outputs precomputed by
data-raw/generate-io-yft-vignette-cache.R instead of rebuilding the
model, so each renders in about 15 s.

