diff --git a/man/io_yft_data.Rd b/man/io_yft_data.Rd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6b643e7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/man/io_yft_data.Rd
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+% Generated by roxygen2: do not edit by hand
+% Please edit documentation in R/data-io-yft.R
+\docType{data}
+\name{io_yft_data}
+\alias{io_yft_data}
+\title{Indian Ocean yellowfin tuna (simulated) assessment data}
+\format{
+A named list of 62 elements in the form \code{\link[=opal_obj]{opal_obj()}} expects:
+dimensions, catch (\code{catch_obs_ysf}), the index (\code{cpue_data}), biology,
+growth settings, length compositions (\verb{lf_*}), the recruitment bias
+adjustment (\code{bias_adj_y}) and priors.
+}
+\source{
+Converted from SS3 v3.24 files with the SS3-to-opal converter in
+\url{https://github.com/N-DucharmeBarth/wcpfc-bet-single-region}
+(\verb{code/rtmb/scripts/04-export-io-yft-for-opal.r}). SS3 model by M.N.
+Maunder, H. Xu and C. Minte-Vera (IATTC); data simulated from the
+operating model described in Goethel et al. (2024)
+\doi{10.1111/faf.12819}.
+}
+\usage{
+io_yft_data
+}
+\description{
+Model inputs for a quarterly, single-region assessment of simulated Indian
+Ocean yellowfin tuna, converted from the IATTC analyst team's Stock
+Synthesis 3 (SS3) model for the Spatial Stock Assessment Simulation
+Experiment (replicate 4). Used by the "Comparing opal with Stock Synthesis"
+article.
+}
+\details{
+The model runs 256 quarterly time steps (\code{n_year = 256}, \code{n_season = 1})
+and SS3 ages 1--28, so the opal age index equals the SS3 age. There are 20
+fisheries: 16 extraction fleets with catch in numbers, and the longline
+CPUE index split into four quarterly series (fisheries 17--20), each with
+its own catchability. Length compositions (5 cm bins) are multinomial for
+fisheries 1--14 and 16, with SS3's \code{mult_by_lencomp_N} carried as
+\code{lf_var_adjust}; \code{\link[=prep_lf_data]{prep_lf_data()}} has already been applied.
+
+Biology is SS3's age-based end-of-run biology: M, weight, maturity and
+spawning potential at age, with M scaled to the quarter. Growth uses SS3's
+\verb{GrowthModel 3} (age-specific K): \code{k_mult_ages} gives the ages with K
+multipliers, which are in \code{io_yft_parameters$log_k_mult}, and
+\code{growth_plus_group_adjust} applies SS3's plus-group length approximation.
+Selectivity is length-based (\code{sel_type_f}: 2 = double normal for fisheries
+1--16, 1 = logistic for the index series). \code{sel_basis_f} is not set, so
+every curve is evaluated on length; adding \code{sel_basis_f = rep(2L, 20)}
+evaluates them on age instead, as SS3 does (see the "Length- or age-based
+selectivity" article). \code{priors} holds the default
+priors from \code{\link[=get_priors]{get_priors()}}.
+}
+\examples{
+data(io_yft_data)
+io_yft_data$n_year
+head(io_yft_data$cpue_data)
+}
+\seealso{
+\link{io_yft_parameters}, \link{io_yft_map}, \link{io_yft_reference}
+}
+\keyword{datasets}
